# Family A26: how the engine calls its lane's ready queue (internal/engine).
# See hack/bakeoff.sh.
PKG=./internal/engine
BENCH=BenchmarkAPI/Dispatch
REF=interface
AUTO_KEY=dispatch
KIND_DIM=""
KINDS_TEST=TestDispatchKindsList
AUTO_FILE=-
ADR=17
TITLE="Variant dispatch mechanism (A26)"
# The engine hosts several variant families, so this one has its own list
# test: hack/bakeoff.sh A26.
#
# A dispatch mechanism is selected by a build tag rather than by a field of
# KindSet, so there is no auto.go to generate (AUTO_FILE=-) and ADR-017 carries
# no auto: front-matter for the family — the same shape as A29, whose copy mode
# is chosen per publication. The mechanism is a path segment of the benchmark
# name rather than a key=value dimension (§10.5 spells BenchmarkAPI/Dispatch
# that way), which is why KIND_DIM is empty.
#
# `make bench-lint PKG=./internal/engine` does not cover this family: the
# linter runs `-run ^TestKindsList$` and does not read KINDS_TEST, so it checks
# the package's primary family (A1's ready queues) and reports "1 family ok".
# A29 has the same gap for the same reason. What covers the three arms instead
# is TestReadyQueueBindsEveryKind plus the native/MPMC differential, and
# `make test-tags`, which runs the whole engine and queue suites under
# -tags iqmq_queue_mpmc and -tags iqmq_queue_native. Teaching the linter to
# read KINDS_TEST is a change to a shared tool that belongs with A29's row,
# not with one family's.
#
# All three arms are measured in one binary, so no EXTRA_ARGS are needed: what
# the tags change is which mechanism the engine itself uses, and that shows up
# in BenchmarkMemory/PubSubAck. To measure the engine under a binding:
#   EXTRA_ARGS="-tags iqmq_queue_mpmc"   hack/bakeoff.sh A1
#   EXTRA_ARGS="-tags iqmq_queue_native" hack/bakeoff.sh A1
#
# The §9 criterion (the API design) is that the interface stays the
# default unless a binding is worth more than 5 % end to end, because a tag
# that binds one kind is a kind the differential tests cover less of.

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="bind default via build tag if > 5% cost"
# MATRIX=default is the only grid: this root has no IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX
# branch. The criterion is a percentage cost of the dispatch mechanism, read
# on the same call in each, which the two parallelism points produce.
MATRIX=default
DECIDED_AT="P=1 P=2"
DECIDED_ON="ns/op allocs/op"
